A||||5||Tabs31||Help With Rims||||1||
Z||000000||Tabs31||11-26-2001||06:25 PM||||I have never bought rims before and I was wondering if you guys and gals could help me out???<P>I was looking at a set of rims and wanted to know if they would fit on my fiero here is the info: the bolt pattern is 5/100mm/4.5 and the off set is +42mm. Also I need tuner lugs??? what are those??? Please help me out <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Heres a pic of the rims <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rims_4_fiero.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tabs31_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pyric||11-26-2001||06:36 PM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.whalentire.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.whalentire.com</A>  they can tell you what size tire your going to need and explain some other things in the "Help" section.<P>But to answer.. That bolt pattern should be fine.  It may stick out of the wheel well some because of the +42mm offset.<P>As for the tuner lugs, they aren't anything special.  They just work more like a screw than a bolt.  It requires a special lug nut adapter. (which means you'll pretty much have locking lug nuts from the start).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Later, <P>------------------<BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown<p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||matt300ZX||11-26-2001||06:39 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.eliteone.com/wheels/ssr.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.eliteone.com/wheels/ssr.htm</A> <BR>These are very similar to mine except they aren't polished and they would look better on your car than the ones you have picked out.||||reg||10
Z||000003||banditbalz||11-26-2001||07:40 PM||||Tabs, I love the rims you got... I'd spend the money on a set of Eibach's first. You keeping the current rims for winter? Love the new paint!||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||11-26-2001||07:54 PM||||Sizing is good, and actually they will stick IN a little bit, due to the greater offset (the larger the offset, the furthur IN a wheel will tuck.)  5x100mm is correct, and a 42mm offset in a 7" wheel is durn near perfect for our cars.   Try to get larger (8" or so) wheels and tyres in the rear, Fieros like an asymetric setup.<P>I like those SSRs, they're nice and light too.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dgzfiero||11-27-2001||06:27 PM|||| I have a question. How do those rims fit a five lug bolt pattern? It doesn't look like it would line up. At least to me anyways.<BR> Doug||||reg||1
